<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian treasury rate rises at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisian treasury rate rises at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury on Tuesday raised 9.0 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated May 20, and repaid maturing paper totalling 33.2 million dinars.</p>
<p>It sold three-year notes payable in equal annual tranches worth nine million dinars at a 7.2500 percent coupon rate, up from 7.1250 percent at May 6 auction.</p>
<p>Banks bid for 49 million dinars for three-, five-year notes at between 7.2500 and 8.1250 percent. (one $=1.08 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
